00:11:12.777 --> 00:11:15.614
up right now wants to have
an organization that's more

00:11:15.614 --> 00:11:19.824
transparent and that you guys
will all solve and tackle and

00:11:19.824 --> 00:11:24.598
move the ball in your causes
but your impact on all the 13 to

00:11:24.598 --> 00:11:26.571
22-year-olds right now
that look up to three or four

00:11:26.571 --> 00:11:29.864
organizations are the most
progressive, that you have been

00:11:29.864 --> 00:11:30.924
at the forefront of,

00:11:30.924 --> 00:11:33.924
I think your impact 
is far greater on

00:11:33.924 --> 00:11:37.084
what you do to the entire
landscape of NGOs

00:11:37.084 --> 00:11:39.059
then just the 
mission you have here.

00:11:39.059 --> 00:11:39.937
- Well, that was the vision.

00:11:39.937 --> 00:11:41.722
The beginning was
to reinvent charity.

00:11:41.722 --> 00:11:43.524
So most people just know
us through the mission--

00:11:43.524 --> 00:11:44.044
- Yep.

00:11:44.044 --> 00:11:45.196
- and I believe those
are very different.

00:11:45.196 --> 00:11:46.972
The mission is to give
clean drinking water.

00:11:46.972 --> 00:11:49.309
Make sure there's a day when
we are not doing this interview

00:11:49.309 --> 00:11:50.674
talking about water.

00:11:50.674 --> 00:11:52.932
All of our kids, who are about
the same age, are growing up.

00:11:52.932 --> 00:11:54.376
- Solve it. Next.

00:11:54.376 --> 00:11:56.943
- My team is not coming in to
their school showing pictures of

00:11:56.943 --> 00:11:58.842
kids drinking nasty water.

00:11:58.842 --> 00:11:59.821
That's the mission.

00:11:59.821 --> 00:12:02.462
But you're right the vision 
was to do charity differently.

00:12:02.462 --> 00:12:04.626
Charity is a virtue.

00:12:04.626 --> 00:12:07.274
There's a lot of talk these
days about good businesses.

00:12:07.274 --> 00:12:08.353
- Right.

00:12:08.353 --> 00:12:12.145
- There is a role and a place
for pure philanthropic capital.

00:12:12.785 --> 00:12:14.769
There are companies out there
that are trying to solve the

00:12:14.769 --> 00:12:17.039
water crisis through
selling bottled water.

00:12:17.039 --> 00:12:20.712
They sell at $2.30 bottle of
water and five cents goes.

00:12:20.712 --> 00:12:22.012
Okay?

00:12:22.012 --> 00:12:24.102
It's better to just get a bunch
of people to give five cents

00:12:24.102 --> 00:12:26.382
instead of buying the water.

00:12:26.382 --> 00:12:27.418
I believe there's
a place for it.

00:12:27.418 --> 00:12:29.951
- Like every model you have 
certain people that start with

00:12:29.951 --> 00:12:32.581
a good mission at hand 
where buy one, give one

00:12:32.581 --> 00:12:34.191
and then every huckster

00:12:34.191 --> 00:12:37.225
comes along and here I want
to raise $15 million for my

00:12:37.225 --> 00:12:40.462
umbrella company. Gary, good
news for everybody who buys an

00:12:40.462 --> 00:12:43.143
umbrella I'm going to give
an umbrella to some kid

00:12:43.143 --> 00:12:44.702
that doesn't need it.

00:12:44.702 --> 00:12:46.500
It becomes
tactics over religion.

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:47.380
- But that was it.

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:49.446
100% of the public's money would
be the way we'd solve it.

00:12:49.446 --> 00:12:53.044
We would go find a group of 
visionary people who didn't

00:12:53.044 --> 00:12:55.929
distrust charity and we can 
get fund the staff and

00:12:55.929 --> 00:12:58.294
the operations that 
we would have.

00:12:58.294 --> 00:13:00.409
That's a group 
of 110 people today,

00:13:00.409 --> 00:13:02.036
many who have been on your show.

00:13:02.036 --> 00:13:03.993
I know you and your wife have
been long-term supporters of

00:13:03.993 --> 00:13:06.174
that but it is a very
simple model:

00:13:06.174 --> 00:13:07.881
there are two bank accounts.

00:13:07.881 --> 00:13:09.538
110 people pay 
for the overhead,

00:13:09.538 --> 00:13:12.483
1 million people have been 
able to give in a pure way.

00:13:12.483 --> 00:13:15.153
So we say you don't trust where
the money's going how about

00:13:15.153 --> 00:13:18.418
this: 100% of your money, we
even pay back credit card fees.

00:13:18.418 --> 00:13:20.845
This costs us hundreds of
thousands of dollars a year so

00:13:20.845 --> 00:13:23.104
if someone were to give $100
bucks on their Amex because

00:13:23.104 --> 00:13:26.597
Lizzie and I you can give your
$17 and every one of them and

00:13:26.597 --> 00:13:28.811
I'm not joking and every
one of those pennies goes--

00:13:28.811 --> 00:13:29.919
- And we don't get 17.

00:13:29.919 --> 00:13:31.541
We get $16.81.
- Yeah.

00:13:31.541 --> 00:13:33.498
- We actually take your
money to make up the difference.

00:13:33.498 --> 00:13:36.029
So that every dollar
can go to the field.

00:13:36.029 --> 00:13:37.787
- Don't steal
those 19 cents, DRock.

00:13:37.787 --> 00:13:41.037
- We just try to connect people
to the impact that was having.

00:13:41.037 --> 00:13:43.667
Because money was not fungible.
- Yes.

00:13:43.667 --> 00:13:45.429
- These bank accounts were
separate and they were audited

00:13:45.429 --> 00:13:47.328
separately we
could track dollars.

00:13:47.328 --> 00:13:51.314
So I could say to a kid, to your
daughter, she did a birthday

00:13:51.314 --> 00:13:54.734
campaign, she can see actual
photos and GPS of those wells.

00:13:54.734 --> 00:13:56.362
- Before we go here and 
I need to move this along.

00:13:56.362 --> 00:13:57.458
The birthday campaign.

00:13:57.458 --> 00:13:59.128
I don't want to miss it
before we get into it.

00:13:59.128 --> 00:14:00.803
This was a monumental thing

00:14:00.803 --> 00:14:02.346
from afar from a
marketing standpoint.

00:14:02.346 --> 00:14:03.508
- We got lucky.
We stumbled into it.

00:14:03.508 --> 00:14:06.836
- But instead of giving the full
story you can look this up and

00:14:06.836 --> 00:14:08.646
Google it but give
them at least what it is.

00:14:08.646 --> 00:14:12.323
- People instead of throwing a
party or accepting gifts because

00:14:12.323 --> 00:14:13.966
we have enough crap 
and we get stuff

00:14:13.966 --> 00:14:15.542
we don't even need 
for our birthday.

00:14:15.542 --> 00:14:16.785
And we don't
really need parties.

00:14:16.785 --> 00:14:18.176
- It's your 33rd birthday,--

00:14:18.176 --> 00:14:20.280
- you donate it and you
ask your age in dollars.

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:23.099
33-year-olds ask for $33.

00:14:23.099 --> 00:14:24.542
- Right so you ask your homies,
you send an email, put up social

00:14:24.542 --> 00:14:26.653
media posts instead of
getting me a gift, give $33.

00:14:26.653 --> 00:14:28.620
- And seven-year-olds 
as for seven dollars and

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:30.245
89-year-olds ask for $89.

00:14:30.245 --> 00:14:32.241
This has helped a
million people get water.

00:14:32.241 --> 00:14:33.536
- I was just going to say,
what has been

00:14:33.536 --> 00:14:34.757
the impact of this campaign?

00:14:34.757 --> 00:14:38.387
- The average for person raises
$1,000 from 15 of their friends.

00:14:38.387 --> 00:14:41.500
So as an idea a million
birthdays could be billion

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:43.018
dollars for clean water.

00:14:43.018 --> 00:14:43.939
- Right because not everybody

00:14:43.939 --> 00:14:46.002
gives just $33 on 
their 33rd birthday.

00:14:46.002 --> 00:14:48.745
- Some add zero,
some give $3.30.

00:14:48.745 --> 00:14:49.898
- Great.
- Every dollar goes in--

00:14:49.898 --> 00:14:51.265
- Who's the first
person to do it?

00:14:51.265 --> 00:14:54.069
- So I was birthday number
one on my 32nd but then this

00:14:54.069 --> 00:14:57.515
seven-year-old kid in Austin
starts knocking on doors and

00:14:57.515 --> 00:14:59.145
he raises 22 grand.

00:14:59.145 --> 00:15:01.446
And then like holy crap.

00:15:01.446 --> 00:15:02.630
And then Jack Dorsey
did three birthdays.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:04.057
And Will Smith
did their birthday.

00:15:04.057 --> 00:15:04.907
- And away we went.

00:15:04.907 --> 00:15:08.295
- And away we went and
89-year-olds No-No Nguyen

00:15:08.295 --> 00:15:09.974
gave up her 89th birthday

00:15:09.974 --> 00:15:11.031
and wrote a mission 
statement and said,

00:15:11.031 --> 00:15:14.031
"You know, I'd like other people
to have chance to turn 89."

00:15:14.031 --> 00:15:15.834
It's a really beautiful idea.

00:15:15.834 --> 00:15:18.387
Our birthdays can help people
actually have more birthdays.

00:15:19.197 --> 00:15:21.694
You can actually pledge
charitywater.org/birthdays/.

00:15:21.694 --> 00:15:22.562
- Link it up.

00:15:22.562 --> 00:15:24.566
- Even if your birthday 
is a year from now.

00:15:24.566 --> 00:15:26.394
You've done them,
I've done seven now.

00:15:26.394 --> 00:15:27.773
Your kid's done one.

00:15:27.773 --> 00:15:28.692
It's a great thing.

00:15:28.692 --> 00:15:30.254
- [India] Half birthdays.
- Half birthdays, I like that.

00:15:30.254 --> 00:15:33.253
- Yeah, I'm 26 and a half--
- and you raise on $26.50?

00:15:33.253 --> 00:15:34.351
- Yeah.
- Done.

00:15:34.351 --> 00:15:35.802
DRock, book it.

00:15:35.802 --> 00:15:37.351
- [India] Actually this segues

00:15:37.351 --> 00:15:38.799
